│ patch_description        │ Replace the degenerate all-zero construction with a deterministic maximin search in       │
│                          │ barycentric coordinates. The equilateral triangle is parameterized by `(u, v)` with `u >= │
│                          │ 0`, `v >= 0`, and `u + v <= 1`; importantly, the absolute determinant of three such       │
│                          │ coordinate pairs is exactly the triangle area normalized by the area of the enclosing     │
│                          │ equilateral triangle.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search fixes the three extremal vertices, which are structurally useful in strong     │
│                          │ Heilbronn configurations, and evolves the remaining points using an elite-preserving      │
│                          │ stochastic search with a fixed seed. Candidate mutations are projected back to the        │
│                          │ simplex, so every returned point is guaranteed to lie within the target triangle.         │
│                          │ Selection uses the minimum normalized area plus a small lower-tail bonus, avoiding        │
│                          │ unstable configurations that improve just one bottleneck triangle while creating several  │
│                          │ nearly degenerate ones.                                                                   │
