│ patch_name               │ deterministic_maximin_search                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the degenerate all-zero construction with a deterministic maximin search in       │
│                          │ barycentric coordinates. The three vertices are retained as anchor points, while the      │
│                          │ remaining eight points are optimized inside the reference simplex using a fixed-seed      │
│                          │ differential-evolution phase followed by a batched local refinement phase.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The objective is evaluated directly as the minimum absolute determinant over all 165      │
│                          │ triples. In barycentric reference coordinates this determinant is exactly the triangle    │
│                          │ area normalized by the area of the enclosing equilateral triangle, avoiding unnecessary   │
│                          │ geometric conversions during optimization. A final affine map converts the best           │
│                          │ reference-simplex arrangement back to the requested equilateral triangle. The fallback    │
│                          │ arrangement ensures a valid result if an unexpected numerical failure occurs.             │
