│ patch_name               │ elitist_differential_annealing                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the independent single-point random walks with a hybrid elitist                   │
│                          │ differential-evolution annealer. The previous population members could only communicate   │
│                          │ through the final saved best layout, so most evaluations explored unrelated local traps.  │
│                          │ The replacement retains every improved individual, uses the current global best as an     │
│                          │ attraction point, and uses differences between successful population members to propose   │
│                          │ scale-aware multi-coordinate moves. Periodic deterministic rejuvenation of the worst      │
│                          │ members around elite layouts prevents premature collapse. This is particularly useful for │
│                          │ the Heilbronn objective, whose active minimum-area constraints change abruptly and        │
│                          │ generally require coordinated motion of several interior points.                          │
