│ patch_name               │ uniform_barycentric_local_refine                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current barycentric decoder is feasible but not area-uniform: sampling its second     │
│                          │ parameter uniformly substantially over-samples the region near the top vertex.            │
│                          │ Transforming that parameter with the inverse triangular-area CDF makes initial candidates │
│                          │ and differential-evolution mutations explore the equilateral container uniformly.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The final refinement currently moves all 16 parameters simultaneously, which becomes      │
│                          │ increasingly unlikely to improve a nonsmooth max-min objective once several nearly active │
│                          │ triangle constraints exist. Use a mixture of one-coordinate, two-coordinate, and global   │
│                          │ perturbations. This permits precise motion of individual points while retaining           │
│                          │ occasional coordinated moves.                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
