│ patch_name               │ continuation_subgradient                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This replaces the genetic population search with a vectorized deterministic continuation  │
│                          │ optimizer. It optimizes many candidate configurations simultaneously using analytic       │
│                          │ gradients of a smooth soft-min approximation to the minimum triangle determinant. The     │
│                          │ smoothing temperature is progressively reduced, turning the objective from a broad        │
│                          │ landscape into the true nonsmooth maximin objective. Points are projected into            │
│                          │ barycentric simplex coordinates after every update, while the three enclosing-triangle    │
│                          │ vertices remain fixed. This avoids expensive selection/mutation cycles and directly       │
│                          │ follows active minimum-area constraints.                                                  │
