│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ staged_differential_elites                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single-scale clone-and-jitter evolution with a staged schedule that preserves │
│                          │ the successful elite mechanism while adding differential recombination during the         │
│                          │ exploratory phase. Pure elite mutation rapidly collapses population diversity, which is   │
│                          │ especially problematic for the nonsmooth Heilbronn maximin landscape because improving    │
│                          │ configurations often require correlated movement of several points. Differential          │
│                          │ proposals preserve such correlations and can escape the basin found by sparse mutation.   │
│                          │ The latter half retains smaller sparse perturbations for active-constraint polishing. The │
│                          │ selection surrogate is also made much closer to the actual minimum-area objective, so     │
│                          │ tail-area tie breaking cannot displace a genuinely better minimum triangle.               │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
