│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ boundaryaware_de11                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces the all-interior free-point encoding with a boundary-aware          │
│                          │ parameterization: the three container vertices are retained, one additional point is      │
│                          │ placed on each side, and five points remain free inside the triangle. This is useful for  │
│                          │ Heilbronn-style configurations because strong solutions frequently use boundary support   │
│                          │ points, while the original continuous encoding is unlikely to discover exact boundary     │
│                          │ points.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search combines vectorized differential evolution with a smooth minimum-area          │
│                          │ surrogate during global exploration. The surrogate rewards improving several              │
│                          │ nearly-active triangle constraints instead of only the current worst triangle, helping    │
│                          │ the population escape nonsmooth plateaus. A deterministic local batch refinement then     │
│                          │ optimizes the true minimum doubled area. The best true configuration is tracked           │
│                          │ independently throughout.                                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
