│ patch_description        │ This version replaces the slow single-point annealing population update with a            │
│                          │ deterministic differential-evolution style population search. Differential evolution      │
│                          │ changes multiple coordinates coherently, allowing it to escape configurations where       │
│                          │ one-point moves cannot improve the currently active minimum-area triangle.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation retains the useful barycentric/simplex coordinate system, fixed        │
│                          │ equilateral-triangle vertices, fully vectorized triangle scoring, deterministic random    │
│                          │ seed, simplex-safe projection, and a final coordinate-level maximin polish. It also       │
│                          │ periodically refreshes poor population members around the current best layout to preserve │
│                          │ diversity without losing the incumbent solution.                                          │
