│ patch_description        │ Replace the degenerate all-zero construction with a deterministic population-based        │
│                          │ maximin search in barycentric coordinates. Three triangle vertices are retained as fixed  │
│                          │ points, while eight interior/boundary points are evolved by differential mutations and    │
│                          │ targeted Gaussian mutations.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The objective is evaluated simultaneously for every population member and all 165         │
│                          │ triples. Since the minimum area is controlled by only a few active constraints, the       │
│                          │ targeted stage identifies points occurring in the currently smallest triangles and        │
│                          │ perturbs precisely those coordinates. This is substantially more effective than uniform   │
│                          │ late-stage noise. Barycentric projection guarantees that every returned point remains in  │
│                          │ the required equilateral triangle, and exact elitism retains the best arrangement         │
│                          │ throughout the fixed-seed search.                                                         │
