│ patch_name               │ staged_softmin_evolution                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce a staged selection objective for the evolutionary phase. The exact minimum-area │
│                          │ objective is highly nonsmooth: most mutations are rejected because they do not            │
│                          │ immediately improve the single active triangle. During the exploratory phase, a stable    │
│                          │ soft minimum rewards layouts that improve several nearly-active triangle constraints      │
│                          │ simultaneously. The final phase returns to exact maximin selection, preserving direct     │
│                          │ optimization of the benchmark metric.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The elite pool, mutation scale, crossover rate, and restart noise are also staged: early  │
│                          │ generations retain diversity and make larger coordinated moves; later generations use a   │
│                          │ much smaller elite pool and more conservative changes to polish a promising basin. The    │
│                          │ incumbent is still always tracked using the exact normalized minimum area.                │
