│ patch_name               │ active_set_de11                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The previous approach used 240 layouts, 3600 generations, unrestricted interior           │
│                          │ coordinates for all eight non-vertex points, and a coordinate-only polish. The new        │
│                          │ construction uses a lower-dimensional and more structured 13-parameter family: three      │
│                          │ points are explicitly constrained to the three container sides, while five remain free in │
│                          │ barycentric coordinates. This makes boundary-supported configurations much easier to      │
│                          │ discover.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The evolutionary phase uses 256 candidates, 1900 generations, an annealed soft-min        │
│                          │ objective early in the search, exact max-min selection late in the search, periodic       │
│                          │ incumbent-centered restarts, and guaranteed elite retention. The final refinement is      │
│                          │ changed from only coordinate directions to active-set perturbations: it detects the point │
│                          │ indices occurring in the currently smallest triangle constraints and preferentially       │
│                          │ perturbs those coordinates. This directly addresses the bottleneck triangles controlling  │
│                          │ the objective.                                                                            │
