│                          │ runtime while the weak support score provides little guidance among configurations with   │
│                          │ nearly equal bottlenecks.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This revision uses a smaller, more efficient 112-member population over 3800 generations, │
│                          │ 20 protected elites, stronger low-area support weighting (0.026), structured              │
│                          │ boundary/interior seeds, and a two-stage search. Early generations retain differential    │
│                          │ moves for basin discovery; later generations add active-constraint-aware offspring that   │
│                          │ preferentially perturb points occurring in the 8 smallest triangles. A final batched      │
│                          │ active-set local polish concentrates small moves on the current limiting triples while    │
│                          │ retaining occasional global sparse moves. This better targets the actual maximin          │
│                          │ constraints while reducing redundant evaluations and expected runtime.                    │
