│ patch_name               │ boundary_island_initialization                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Add two deterministic near-boundary initialization islands while retaining the existing   │
│                          │ fully interior Dirichlet population and the structured grid seeds. In normalized          │
│                          │ barycentric coordinates, strong Heilbronn layouts often have useful hull/near-edge        │
│                          │ structure, but putting several points exactly on a side creates zero-area collinear       │
│                          │ triples. The new islands therefore set one randomly selected barycentric weight of each   │
│                          │ movable point to a small strictly positive value, keeping every movable point inside the  │
│                          │ simplex.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ One island is predominantly near-edge, and another is mixed interior/near-edge. This      │
│                          │ broadens the explored combinatorial families without changing feasibility, the objective, │
│                          │ or the later evolutionary and polishing mechanisms. The original random population        │
│                          │ remains present, so this only adds structured diversity rather than committing the search │
│                          │ to a boundary-heavy family.                                                               │
