│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ late_active_set_mutation                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Reserve a late-search offspring class for constraints that actually limit the current     │
│                          │ configuration. The existing mutation perturbs every coordinate of every candidate, which  │
│                          │ is useful for broad exploration but becomes inefficient after the population has found a  │
│                          │ reasonably structured arrangement. During the final third of each island search, this     │
│                          │ edit identifies the twelve smallest-area triples of selected parent configurations, finds │
│                          │ the non-vertex points participating in those triples, and applies a substantially smaller │
│                          │ perturbation only to those points. This directly targets the active constraints           │
│                          │ responsible for the current minimum area while retaining the original differential and    │
│                          │ full-coordinate Gaussian mutations for the majority of candidates.                        │
