│ patch_description        │ Add a late-generation active-set offspring class. In maximin triangle arrangements,       │
│                          │ progress near the optimum is controlled by the small collection of currently limiting     │
│                          │ triples rather than by the entire point set. The existing mutation is unbiased and useful │
│                          │ globally, but it becomes inefficient once the search reaches the approximately 0.03       │
│                          │ regime.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ During the final 32% of generations, this edit reserves 28% of offspring for a small,     │
│                          │ sparse perturbation directed at the free point appearing most frequently among each       │
│                          │ offspring's twelve smallest-area triples. The perturbation remains random and             │
│                          │ deterministic under the existing seeded RNG, but concentrates search effort on            │
│                          │ coordinates responsible for active constraints. Its scale is substantially smaller than   │
│                          │ global mutation, preserving the delicate near-feasible separation achieved by elite       │
│                          │ inheritance. The original unbiased mutation remains in place for all offspring,           │
│                          │ maintaining global exploration and avoiding premature convergence to a particular         │
│                          │ active-set pattern.                                                                       │
