│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ plateau_aware_active_polish                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Strengthen the deterministic local phase rather than spending additional time on broad    │
│                          │ random search.  Maximin configurations commonly lie on plateaus: a one-coordinate LP move │
│                          │ can preserve the current minimum area while increasing the next several nearly-active     │
│                          │ areas, thereby enabling a later coordinate move to improve the true minimum.  The current │
│                          │ code rejects all such moves and uses a random coordinate order.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit accepts objectively neutral coordinate moves only when the existing lower-tail  │
│                          │ surrogate improves, so the exact objective cannot materially regress while plateaus are   │
│                          │ traversed monotonically.  It also prioritizes free points which occur most often among    │
│                          │ the current fifteen smallest triangles, directly attacking the active constraint set.     │
│                          │ More coordinate passes allow these plateau transitions to propagate through the           │
│                          │ configuration.                                                                            │
